  Status: author draft. This unit has not yet had independent mathematical or
  Lean-correspondence review. Source revision inspected:
  <verbatim|3456e5e75cf8d4cd558955a5c7638fba2d68f464>.

  <section|Scope><label|scope>

  The prose is <verbatim|manuscript/existence/centered-budget.tex>. It proves
  the exact finite-volume conversion from a radial transfer lane and its
  stopping-depth bill to a centered copied-product root estimate, including
  the all-site translation step. It states the lane price estimate as a local
  input; its proof is now in <verbatim|manuscript/existence/centered-production.tex>.
  The upstream production of ready/covering schedules and service
  certificates remains open.

  The output matches the <verbatim|centeredBudget> target: for a grade
  <verbatim|g> label, one centered tiling at depth <verbatim|m>, all sites,
  chamber interiority, and root test bounded by the specified right-hand
  side. In the source <verbatim|YM.Extraction.Wcmain> has one eventual volume
  tail that works for every period, so the same source estimate supplies both
  fixed-period and expanding-period budgets by restriction. The prose keeps
  this quantifier order explicit.

  <section|Exact source correspondence><label|exact-source-correspondence>

  <block|<tformat|<twith|table-width|1par>|<twith|table-hmode|exact>|<cwith|1|-1|1|-1|cell-hyphen|t>|<cwith|1|1|1|-1|cell-bborder|1ln>|<cwith|1|1|1|-1|cell-valign|bottom>|<table|<row|<cell|<strong|Prose
  component>>|<cell|<strong|Pinned declarations and
  paths>>|<cell|<strong|Checked correspondence>>>|<row|<cell|Finite-volume
  lane and transfer conditions>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.Overlay.Lane>,
  <verbatim|.Works>, <verbatim|.signal>, <verbatim|.from_>;
  <verbatim|Lean/YM/Overlay/Engine.lean>>|<cell|A lane has a slab family at
  each level, marker loads and actual configuration functions.
  <verbatim|Works> asserts admissibility, active radial data at every level
  from its stop to terminal scale, parent compatibility of origins,
  integrability, the terminal identity, and the recursive transfer equation.
  Induction down the finite sequence identifies the full-mode normalized
  moment with the terminal lane product; there is no limiting
  step.>>|<row|<cell|Exact radial budget>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.Overlay.Bands.Radial>;
  <verbatim|Lean/YM/Overlay/Table.lean>>|<cell|<verbatim|pure>: every marker
  weight is positive. <verbatim|localU>: weight times local coefficient norm
  is at most <verbatim|u>. <verbatim|factor>: <verbatim|b\<gtr\>0>.
  <verbatim|bulk>: nonnegative <verbatim|t_i> bound each positive-ray
  coefficient on its healthy support; the weighted toll times support-mass
  charges have per-origin <verbatim|SumBudget c>. <verbatim|hits>:
  nonnegative <verbatim|t_{ij}> bound each marked interaction coefficient
  pointwise; their weighted toll and forced-support charges have per-origin
  <verbatim|SumBudget (d*b)>. The prose renames the hit coefficient
  <verbatim|d> as <verbatim|gamma> to avoid confusing it with observable
  grade.>>|<row|<cell|Radial data controls the lane
  moment>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.Overlay.Lane.pays>;
  <verbatim|Lean/YM/Overlay/Engine.lean>; <verbatim|Bands.bulkBound>,
  <verbatim|.baseBound>, <verbatim|.population>, <verbatim|.physical>,
  <verbatim|.material>, <verbatim|.total> in
  <verbatim|Lean/YM/Overlay/Pays.lean>, <verbatim|Bill.lean>; detailed proof
  in <verbatim|centered-production.tex>>|<cell|The source first sums the
  per-origin budgets using nonempty ray/forced supports, obtains absolute
  summability and total price bounds, bounds the full subset expansion by
  <verbatim|exp(sum of prices)>, integrates the density, and divides by the
  positive vacuum denominator. <verbatim|Lane.pays> yields the product of the
  scalar blocking monomial, the norm of the normalized full-mode moment, and
  the full-mode polynomial toll, bounded by the exponential of
  <verbatim|Bands.finalBill>. The production unit proves the absolute-price
  and denominator estimates; this unit applies the resulting lane price
  estimate.>>|<row|<cell|Extensive cost conversion>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.Vac.suffices_bill>,
  <verbatim|YM.Vac.treasury>; <verbatim|Lean/YM/Vac/Treasury.lean>;
  <verbatim|Bands.finalBill> in <verbatim|Lean/YM/Overlay/Bill.lean>>|<cell|The
  final bill is bounded by the number of fine sites times the per-site
  treasury plus <verbatim|q(u+c+gamma*b)>, where <verbatim|q> is marker
  count. For markers filling the depth-<verbatim|m> torus,
  <verbatim|q=\|Lambda_m\|>. The exact four-dimensional site-count identity
  is <verbatim|\|Lambda_r\|=\|Lambda_m\|(a_m/a_r)^4>.>>|<row|<cell|Root
  extraction>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.Stock.est>;
  <verbatim|YM.Cells.Tiling.rootTest>, <verbatim|.powering>;
  <verbatim|Lean/YM/Overlay/Terminal.lean>,
  <verbatim|Lean/YM/Cells/Tiling.lean>>|<cell|The full centered mode has one
  copy per cell. Its moment is <verbatim|M>; the root test is
  <verbatim|\|\|M\|\|^(1/\|Lambda_m\|)>. The lane scalar is
  <verbatim|(a_r^g)^\|Lambda_m\|>, and the constant weight toll is
  <verbatim|W^\|Lambda_m\|>. Taking the positive root gives exactly
  <verbatim|exp((a_m/a_r)^4*tau_r+u+c+gamma*b-g log(a_r)-log W)>. Since
  <verbatim|a_r=exp(-scale(r))>, the grade term is <verbatim|g
  scale(r)>.>>|<row|<cell|All-site chamber interiority and
  translations>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.Stock.clear_interior>,
  <verbatim|YM.Stock.translate_s>; <verbatim|Lean/YM/Overlay/Supplier.lean>,
  <verbatim|Lean/YM/Overlay/Terminal.lean>>|<cell|A fixed finite stencil fits
  inside the centered chamber for every period and site once volume is
  sufficiently large. The centered moment/root is translation invariant under
  the specified positive-chamber interiority condition, so an origin estimate
  gives all-site centered budgets.>>|<row|<cell|Finite-prefix
  absorption>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.Stock.Stops.centering>;
  <verbatim|Lean/YM/Overlay/Supplier.lean>>|<cell|From an eventual bill bound
  <verbatim|bill_m \<less\>= (g+eta) scale(m)>, take <verbatim|A> to be one
  plus the finite sum of early-depth ratios
  <verbatim|exp(bill_m)/exp((g+eta)scale(m))>. Later depths have ratio at
  most one. The same <verbatim|A> is independent of period and volume if the
  stop data is.>>|<row|<cell|Upstream actual stop and lane
  producer>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.Stock.Fuel.record>,
  <verbatim|YM.Stock.Stops.works>, <verbatim|YM.Input.Metered.rootwise>,
  <verbatim|YM.Extra.Multi.metered>; <verbatim|Lean/YM/Overlay/Prior.lean>,
  <verbatim|Supplier.lean>, <verbatim|Assembly.lean>,
  <verbatim|Lean/YM/Extra/MULTISOURCE_BOUNDS/Application.lean>>|<cell|<verbatim|Fuel.record>
  turns <verbatim|Fuel.covers> and the schedule's pay estimate into the
  eventual bill inequality; <verbatim|Stops.works> requires a stop-indexed
  sequence of service certificates. The production unit spells out the scale
  arithmetic in <verbatim|Fuel.record> but does not prove
  <verbatim|Fuel.ready>/<verbatim|Fuel.covers> or construct their lanes. The
  producer chain is <verbatim|Extra.Multi.metered> \<rightarrow\>
  <verbatim|Input.Metered.rootwise> \<rightarrow\> <verbatim|Stops.centering>
  \<rightarrow\> <verbatim|Wcmain>. <verbatim|Extra.Multi.metered> requires
  <verbatim|C.Makes>, <verbatim|Prepared> (including factorial/tabs),
  eventual <verbatim|Thick>, and <verbatim|Offer> (plus gauge simplicity);
  these remain upstream obligations.>>>>>

  <section|Exact conclusion and limits><label|exact-conclusion-and-limits>

  The conversion proves a finite-volume estimate for a given transfer lane.
  Its important numerical factors are all explicit: <verbatim|a_r^g> once per
  copied marker, <verbatim|W> once per marker, the site-count ratio
  <verbatim|(a_m/a_r)^4>, and the additive radial cost
  <verbatim|u+c+gamma*b>. No factor depending on the number of
  transfer-matrix states is inserted. The lane needs to fill the entire
  centered cell set so the root exponent agrees with the full-mode marker
  count.

  The remaining substantive task is to prove the actual stop package from its
  RG prerequisites: a lane service certificate for all bounded labels and all
  periods, plus an eventual stopping-depth bill bound of <verbatim|(g+eta)
  scale(m)>. The section records that requirement but does not infer it from
  the existence of a lane or from <verbatim|C.Makes> alone.

  <section|Checks><label|checks>

  <\itemize-minus>
    <item>Inspected the declarations above and their immediate dependencies
    with targeted <verbatim|rg> and <verbatim|sed>; no Lean source was
    changed.

